  "question": {
    "text": "An electron of a stationary hydrogen atom (mass =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>)&nbsp;jumps from the fifth energy level to the ground level. As a result, the atom emits a photon and recoils with some velocity. The velocity that the atom acquires as a result of photon emission is [<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>&nbsp;= Planck's constant,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;= Rydberg's constant]"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>hR</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi>hR</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi>hR</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>hR</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>hc</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>Rhc</mi><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>Rhc</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>hc</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac></math><br />(where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>Rydberg's constant,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo></math>Planck's constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo></math>speed of light in vacuum)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />But&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi>mλ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>Rh</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>"
